  fallenCairn: {fileID: 8505107523154037745, guid: 329b897876476034a9b2c97b975cae6b, type: 3}
  griefLines:
  - I keep looking for {0} at the fire.
  - You came back. {0} didn't. I know how it goes out there. I still don't like it.
  - We put up stones for {0}. It isn't much.
  - Nobody here says it, but we all count who comes back through that portal. {0}... well.
  - Someone saw {0} out there, walking in circles. Walking. Do you understand? Go and look.
  griefRaids: 2
  bosses:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9b7313d497a67e54b8b12e51990184bb, type: 2}
  bondRanks:
  - name: Trusted
    raids: 3
    healthBonus: 0.15
    damageBonus: 0.1
  - name: Sworn
    raids: 8
    healthBonus: 0.3
    damageBonus: 0.2
  memoryLines:
  - kind: 6
    lines:
    - I keep hearing it fall. I think I always will. Good. It should be remembered that it can be done.
    - We killed it. You and me. I didn't think I'd ever say that about anything out there.
  - kind: 5
    lines:
    - You came back for me. Out there, with all of that around you. I won't forget it.
    - I was on the ground and I heard you coming. That's the only reason I'm talking to you now.
  - kind: 1
    lines:
    - We should never have gone that deep. I'm glad you're breathing.
    - It went badly. It goes badly sometimes. We go again when you're ready.
  - kind: 4
    lines:
    - I've stopped checking whether you're behind me. You always are.
    - You know how I fight now, and I know how you do. That's worth more than a good sword.
  - kind: 3
    lines:
    - Another minute out there and we'd both be part of that forest.
    - I felt that portal close behind us. Let's not do that again.
  - kind: 2
    lines:
    - My arms are still shaking. We gave them something to think about.
    - That was a lot of them. We were better.
  memoryReturnsEvery: 2
  foundComesHomeWithin: 20
  lostReportLine: The forest doesn't kill the lost. It forgets them, and they forget everything else. They are out there, and they won't know you.
  foundFollowLine: '{0} doesn''t know you, or their own name. They follow anyway. Get them to an exit alive.'
  foundReportLine: '{0} came home with you, and remembers none of it.'
  leftBehindLine: You found {0}, and left them out there. They will still be walking.
  strangerLines:
  - You keep looking at me as if I should know you. I'm sorry. I don't. They tell me you came back for me. Thank you, whoever you are.
  - They say this is home. They say you brought me back to it. I believe them, I suppose. I don't remember the fire. I don't remember you.
  - I know how to hold a blade and not where I learned it. Everyone here calls me by a name. I've started answering to it.
  returningLines:
  - kind: 1
    lines:
    - We ran from something, didn't we? You and I, with nothing to show for it. I woke up remembering how it felt.
  - kind: 2
    lines:
    - There was a fight. A bad one, back to back. I can still feel it in my arm. That was you beside me. That was you.
  - kind: 3
    lines:
    - I dreamed of a beacon and a clock running out, and you shouting at me to move. That wasn't a dream, was it?
  - kind: 4
    lines:
    - Something came back to me last night. The day I decided you could be trusted. I don't know how I ever stopped.
  - kind: 5
    lines:
    - I was on the ground once, bleeding, and someone hauled me up. Your hands. I remember your hands.
  - kind: 6
    lines:
    - That great rotten thing in the hollow. We killed it, you and me. How does a person forget a thing like that?
  allBackLine: That's the last of it, I think. Every raid, every road, you. Whatever the forest took, it didn't get to keep it.
